# Git workflow

The single source for *how* git is done here. Branch → commit → PR → review → merge.
**Never commit directly to the default branch.**

## Branch

```bash
{% if issue_tracker != "none" -%}
git checkout -b <type>/{{ issue_prefix | lower }}-<N>-<slug>
{%- else -%}
git checkout -b <type>/<slug>
{%- endif %}
```

- **Types:** `feature/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `refactor/`, `docs/`, `test/`, `ci/`, `hotfix/`.
{% if issue_tracker != "none" -%}
- `<N>` = issue number; `<slug>` = kebab-case from the issue title, ≤ 30 chars.
{% else -%}
- `<slug>` = short kebab-case description of the change.
{% endif -%}
- One branch per unit of work. Never work on the default branch.

## Commit

[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>
```

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `style`, `perf`, `ci`, `revert`.
- Subject ≤ 72 chars, imperative mood, no trailing period.
- The body explains **why**, not what.
- Commit in coherent units — one per task or inseparable batch, not one giant dump.

## Pull request

```bash
git push origin <branch>
```

Open the PR against the **default branch**.

- **Title:** Conventional-Commit style{% if issue_tracker != "none" %}, ending with `({{ issue_prefix }}-N)`{% endif %}.
{% if issue_tracker != "none" -%}
- **Body:** include a line of its own — `Closes {{ issue_prefix }}-N`{% if issue_tracker == "github" %} (or `Closes #N`){% endif %}. Use `Refs {{ issue_prefix }}-N` for a partial PR that should not auto-close the issue.
{% endif -%}
- **Template:** fill **every** section of `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`. Never delete a
  section — write "N/A" when it doesn't apply.
- Show the user the PR URL.

### Draft → ready

For a PR opened early as a draft (e.g. during `execute-tasks`): promoting draft → ready is
**not** a push and does not re-trigger push-gated CI. Open it ready, or push again when you
promote it. Drop any `WIP:` prefix and complete the template before marking ready.

## Pre-PR checklist

- [ ] Branch follows the naming rule; not the default branch.
- [ ] Commits are Conventional and scoped to the work.
- [ ] Verification passed with cited evidence (see the verify gate).
- [ ] PR template fully filled{% if issue_tracker != "none" %}; `Closes`/`Refs` line present{% endif %}.

## Anti-patterns (never)

- Committing straight to the default branch.
- A single catch-all commit for unrelated changes.
- Opening a PR with the template half-filled or sections deleted.
{% if issue_tracker != "none" -%}
- A PR that closes an issue without the `Closes {{ issue_prefix }}-N` line.
{% endif -%}
